    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0152" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg40"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6857: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Legation in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-04T11:00:00+08:00">February 4, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 4—6:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. 1. An American adviser has confidentially outlined to Atcheson<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d45-f1"/> the following dark picture drawn from conversations with
                    important figures in Chinese Government and political life: There is no question
                    that Japan is determined to dominate the Chinese affairs and will succeed and
                    there is already evident swing in sentiment among many influential Chinese in
                    Govermnent tending toward antiforeignism with respect to Americans and
                    Europeans; that only three Chinese leaders know the exact nature of Japanese
                    proposals—Chiang Kaishek, Madam Chiang and one other informant could not name;
                    that Japanese proposals together with financial crisis and what informant called
                    foredoomed face [<hi rendition="#italic">fate?</hi>] of Szechwan anticommunist
                    campaign have placed Chiang in inextricable position; and that capitulation to
                    Japanese will lead to his downfall and probably assassination with chaos in
                    China the result.</p>
                <p>2. I feel above is basically true but perhaps overpessimistic.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
